  "full_original_abstract_TeX": "We give a smooth autonomous observed system on a connected closed genus-three\nsurface whose exact finite-time differential observation Gramian is complete\nand has constant negative sectional curvature, although every attained output\nhistory corresponds to exactly two initial states. The system has zero dynamics\nand a Euclidean-valued output obtained by composing a connected double cover of\na closed hyperbolic surface with a smooth Nash isometric embedding into\n$\\R^{17}$. For each fixed $T>0$ its Gramian is $P_T=T\\pi^*g$ and its curvature is\n$-1/T$. Uniform positive upper and lower bounds hold in a fixed finite\nnormalized atlas and relative to any fixed smooth background metric. This\nrefutes the manifold implication printed in Krener's 2009 open problem under\nthose coherent meanings of its coordinate bounds. The construction is an application of classical constructions. A bounded\nprimary-source audit found no earlier explicit complete construction in the\ninspected corpus; no absolute historical firstness is asserted.",
  "full_distinct_native_Description_HTML": "<p>We give a nonvacuous two-dimensional counterexample to the manifold conjecture printed by Krener in OWR11/2009. A smooth observed system on a connected closed genus-three surface has zero dynamics and output in R17 obtained by composing a connected two-sheeted hyperbolic covering with a smooth Nash isometric embedding. Its exact finite-time differential observation Gramian is P_T=T*pi^*g. For every fixed positive T it is geodesically complete with actual sectional curvature -1/T and uniform positive upper and lower bounds relative to any fixed smooth background metric and a fixed finite normalized atlas. The history map is locally injective but every attained history has exactly two initial states.</p><p>The construction is an application of classical constructions, with Nash, covering classification, hyperbolic geometry and older local/global observability ambiguity explicitly credited. A bounded primary-source audit, including complete readings of Dirr2009 and Kang2013 and a fresh independent adversarial priority assessment, found no verified earlier explicit complete construction in inspected sources. Those two named access gaps are closed; older uninspected originals and corpus limits are documented. No absolute firstness, continuous seventeen-year openness, new covering/Nash mechanism, or first refutation of every literal dimensional reading is claimed. A strengthened question restricted to one global Euclidean state domain is outside this result.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in solving, drafting, reproducing and adversarially reviewing the work. This is an unrefereed preprint without conventional human peer review. The package provides the analytical proof and a dependency-free supplementary exact verifier with recorded results, source and priority supplement, reproducibility instructions, license and file digests. Finite controls do not construct a Nash embedding or machine-certify global topology or completeness.</p>",
